# Playback timestamp format

The visible media clock is **`formatHHMMSS`** from `@podverse/helpers` (or `@podverse/helpers/time`).
That is the same helper the progress bar uses. Style: **`1:19:59`**, **`1:05`**, **`0:00`**. Hours
appear only at 3600s+. **Never** zero-pad the first unit (`01:19:59` / `01:05` is wrong).

It accepts a number or a DTO string of seconds (`start_time`, `end_time`).

## Do

```ts
formatHHMMSS(positionSeconds);
formatHHMMSS(chapter.start_time);
formatHHMMSS(Number(chapter.end_time));
```

Web clip/chapter ranges go through `ReadableTimeRange`, which already calls `formatHHMMSS`.

## Don't

- `formatPlaybackTime` at a UI callsite — it is only a null-safe string adapter for the same clock
- `formatClock` — it never switches to `H:MM:SS` and always pads minutes (`01:05`, `60:00`)
- `formatNumericToHHMMSS` as a second display helper — it delegates to `formatHHMMSS`
- A local `padStart` clock or a second `MM:SS` / `HH:MM:SS` helper
- `formatDateTimeAbbrev` for playhead / clip / chapter / transcript clocks

Web, mobile, embed, and any later surface share this helper so a chapter at 4512s cannot read
`01:15:12` on one surface and `1:15:12` on another.
